---
description: Backend (FastAPI + scraping engine) conventions
globs: apps/firescrapling/backend/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- Routes go in `api_server.py`: validate input with a pydantic model, call into `core`
  (`main.py`), shape the response. No scraping or SQL in the route body.
- Auth is a dependency, never inline: `Depends(get_api_context)` for API-key routes,
  `Depends(get_session_user)` for account routes (both in `api_auth.py`).
- Call `_check_target_url(url)` (which wraps `validate_request_url`) before fetching any
  user-supplied URL.
- DB access uses `_get_db()` and parameterised SQL — never string-formatted values.
  Commit before calling another helper that opens its own connection; SQLite permits one
  writer at a time.
- Record billable work with `record_api_usage(...)` after committing, passing the
  endpoint path so `/v1/usage/summary` can aggregate it.
- Long work belongs in the job generators (`scrape_page_streaming`,
  `crawl_site_streaming`), which yield `{"type": "status"|"result"|"error"|"done"}`
  events and persist logs/progress as they go.
- Fetching goes through `fetch_with_retries`; Playwright is only for browser `actions`
  or screenshots. Respect robots.txt and the politeness delay in crawl paths.
- Keep `openapi.yaml` in sync with any route or schema change.
- Type hints on every new function; `from __future__ import annotations` where the file
  already has it.
